From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 09:49:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0266 part 1: a question asking leave to send does not excuse
 an unsent introduction
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The tester's 58043, run 51403: „სთხოვე ზურაბ მელაძეს, დამაკავშიროს
თამარ ხუციშვილთან." was answered „…მივწერო ზურაბს და სთხოვო,
დაგაკავშიროთ?". Nothing went, and the owner never heard that Zurab had not
opened the app. The unsent-instruction guard steps aside when an
introduction run ends with a question, which is right for the reason
question (3697) and wrong for one asking leave to send: the typed
instruction is itself that yes (CF, §139). The guard now holds unless the
last question asks something other than leave to send. With the guard
on, the server's own path gives the approved never-opened line.

No model-facing text changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
